# ============================================================================
# Line endings for generated files.
#
# `src/bindings.ts` is a build artifact: it is written by a Rust exporter that
# always emits LF, and a CI step regenerates it and fails if the result differs
# from what is committed. Under `core.autocrlf=true` (the default on Windows) a
# fresh checkout would hand that step a CRLF file, so the diff would report a
# difference on every run for a file that is in fact up to date -- a gate that
# always fails is worse than no gate. Pin the endings instead of relying on
# every machine's local git config.
# ============================================================================
src/bindings.ts text eol=lf
